n ice water bath. When cool, peel off skin. (15 minutes to cook, 5 seconds to peel each cooked potato) And now, an epic demonstration of How to Peel 2 Pounds of Potatoes in Under A Minute using a drill, (clean) toilet brush, bucket, and water hose. GAME. CHANGER.\\\\n\\\\npassage 2:This versatile medium-starch spud has a delicious, buttery flavor. It cooks up tender and holds its shape, but it also has just enough starch to contribute creaminess without making a potato salad mushy. Its skin can be tough and papery, so we recommend peeling them first.\\\\n\\\\npassage 3:Especially if you are peeling a crap load of potatoes. Here is the easiest way (or at least the easiest way I’ve discovered) to peel a cooked potato. Step 1.) Bring a pot of water to a boil. Step 2.) With a knife, score your potatoes all the way around the center. Step 3.) Place your potatoes in the pot and boil for about 15 minutes or so. Step 4.) Prepare a bowl of ice water and place your potatoes in the water. Step 5.) Swish it around for a few seconds just enough so that it’s cool enough to handle. Step 6.) Remove your potatoe from the water and remove the skin.\\\\n\\\\n\\\",\\\"question\\\":\\\"how to boil potatoes for easy peeling\\\"}\", \"original_answer\": \"To boil potatoes for easy peeling, bring a pot of water to a boil and score your potatoes all the way around the center.\", \"source_sentence_offsets\": [{\"end_byte\": 78, \"source_sentence_id\": 0, \"start_byte\": 0, \"text_sha256\": \"sha256:655c88f5e996aa0090ef9a0e20a98c83e29704de92975fd4d08aa227156207a2\"}, {\"end_byte\": 104, \"source_sentence_id\": 1, \"start_byte\": 78, \"text_sha256\": \"sha256:2456992f5d934a1245004d1832cfd82792477f2df9428a4826719b2bfe21bec2\"}, {\"end_byte\": 309, \"source_sentence_id\": 2, \"start_byte\": 104, \"text_sha256\": \"sha256:73bba26dd75441985f6ad6ba68f1399fbfdd3a2363bf27201842a91f6745ff70\"}, {\"end_byte\": 315, \"source_sentence_id\": 3, \"start_byte\": 309, \"text_sha256\": \"sha256:0c0b0fb669670e